{
  "_comment": "Polish (pl) string bundle for the Python board UI. Any key omitted here falls back to the English source in en.json. Keep every key that en.json defines translated so no English leaks into the Polish UI (guarded by test_i18n). Polish is longer than English and inflects heavily: lines drawn on the 128px e-paper panel are kept short and broken with an explicit newline rather than abbreviated. Two placeholders are filled with a nominative colour label from chess.color.* ('Białe'/'Czarne'), which no Polish verb governs, so lichess.started and game.resign_color label the side instead of inflecting it. Counted nouns after a number use the 's'/'min' symbol rather than a spelt-out noun, because Polish needs three different endings (1 sekunda, 2 sekundy, 5 sekund) and the substituted value is not known here. Every string was measured through the widget that draws it (scripts/measure_locale_fit.py); splash.starting is the one that still sets at 16pt instead of 18pt, kept because 'Uruchamianie' is the word a Polish reader expects for a system starting and the alternative that fits at full size ('Startowanie') is not, and Overflow.FIT shrinks rather than loses text. The register is informal (ty/twój), as Polish consumer products and Lichess's own Polish UI use.",
